---
// Search Console organic revenue — the mockup for key-features.md feature 3
// ("Search Console SEO Revenue Signals").
//
// Replaces public/images/features/feature-3.png, which was the PowerAI TEMPLATE's stock
// "Income Overview" panel: violet progress bars against Mon-Thu and a "$128,653k" figure.
// It was not this product, and its numbers were not anyone's.
//
// ── CHROME PORTED, COLUMNS RE-KEYED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The panel chrome follows dashboard/src/components/GscQueryFixture.jsx, but the columns
// deliberately do NOT. That fixture renders Search Console's QUERY table (query / clicks /
// impressions / CTR / position) and carries no revenue column at all — which does not match
// this feature's copy, whose whole claim is "match organic landing pages and date ranges
// against revenue webhooks."
//
// The surface that actually makes that claim is dashboard/src/pages/SEORevenue.jsx, and it is
// LANDING-PAGE keyed: Landing Page Path / Conversions / Revenue / GSC Clicks / Impressions
// (:197-202). These four columns are that table, trimmed to what stays legible at this card's
// width. Impressions is the column dropped — it is the least load-bearing for the copy.
//
// ── THE TRUTH LABEL IS NOT A FOOTNOTE ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// Revenue here is ESTIMATED, and the panel has to say so. §6: query-level revenue is matched
// by landing page + date range and must carry the truth label; never imply exact
// query -> customer attribution. The real page carries the same disclosure in its "Aggregated
// Data Notice" (SEORevenue.jsx:314), and the column header says "Est. Revenue" rather than
// "Revenue" for the same reason. Removing either would make this mockup a claim the product
// itself refuses to make.
//
// ── THE NUMBERS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Sample data, badged as such — a drawing of the product, not a claim about anyone's data.
// Internally consistent by construction: revenue is conversions x $120, and the click counts
// are GscQueryFixture's own (1,284 / 942 / 631 / 418) so the two panels do not invent two
// different sets of traffic for the same site.
const pages = [
  { path: "/blog/attribution-guide", conversions: "18", revenue: "$2,160", clicks: "1,284" },
  { path: "/compare/ga4", conversions: "12", revenue: "$1,440", clicks: "942" },
  { path: "/docs/install", conversions: "7", revenue: "$840", clicks: "631" },
  { path: "/blog/ai-referral-tracking", conversions: "5", revenue: "$600", clicks: "418" },
];

const totalOrganicRevenue = `$${pages.reduce((sum, p) => sum + Number(p.revenue.replace(/[$,]/g, "")), 0).toLocaleString()}`;
---

<div class="relative z-1 overflow-hidden rounded-[20px] border border-[#3D3830] bg-[#12100C]">
  <!-- Header -->
  <div
    class="flex h-[44px] items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b border-white/10 bg-[#1B1811] px-4"
  >
    <span class="truncate text-xs font-bold text-[#F6F3EB]">
      Search Console — organic revenue
    </span>
    <span
      class="inline-flex flex-shrink-0 items-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-2.5 py-1 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-primary"
      >Sample data</span
    >
  </div>

  <!-- Hero summary header line -->
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[#3D3830] bg-[#18150F] px-4 py-3">
    <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#A79E8C]">Est. Organic Revenue</span>
    <span class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-primary">{totalOrganicRevenue}</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Landing-page table -->
  <div class="overflow-x-auto p-4">
    <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
      <thead>
        <tr
          class="border-b border-[#3D3830] text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-[#7C7568]"
        >
          <th class="py-2 pr-2 font-black">Landing page</th>
          <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right font-black">Conv.</th>
          <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right font-black">Est. revenue</th>
          <th class="py-2 pl-2 text-right font-black">GSC clicks</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          pages.map((p) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-[#3D3830] font-bold last:border-0">
              <td class="max-w-[150px] truncate py-2.5 pr-2 font-mono text-[11px] text-[#F6F3EB]">
                {p.path}
              </td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-2 text-right tabular-nums text-[#D5D0C3]">{p.conversions}</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-2 text-right tabular-nums text-primary">{p.revenue}</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pl-2 text-right tabular-nums text-[#A79E8C]">{p.clicks}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!-- Truth label — §6, and the product's own disclosure -->
  <div class="mx-4 mb-4 rounded-2xl border border-[#3D3830] bg-[#241F17] p-3.5">
    <div class="mb-1 text-[10px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#A79E8C]">
      Estimated
    </div>
    <p class="text-[10px] leading-normal text-[#A79E8C]">
      Matched by landing page and date range. Search Console reports aggregate query data, not
      user-level query&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;customer identity.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
